a.common('Specify and test a new exhibit card','Write a complete contract, choose separate checks and show expected behaviour for supplied and absent evidence.',[(12,'W1 · Replace vague wishes with observable requirements','Use the supplied C/P1 reference and explain each design choice.'),(13,'W2 · Score format and evidence separately','A passing layout does not excuse an invented time.'),(14,'W3 · Preserve a conflict without losing agreed facts','Use P2 and the explicit equally authoritative source disagreement.'),(16,'W5 · Design a fairer small prompt comparison','Retain all trials and use the same cases, criteria and recorded conditions.')], 'In the paper story studio, A passes the three stated checks: three sentences, fox/boat/pond, and no real-person or real-event claim. B includes the required three elements but has two sentences and asserts a real event involving the teacher; it fails the sentence-count and no-real-event checks. The story task permits additional fictional events, unlike the source-only factual card. Partner outputs must be scored under the same rubric and retained, not invented. Paper trials do not establish model reliability. Reserve Specify and test a new exhibit card for an independent first attempt.',{12:[r]})
